---
import { danubeImage, budaCastleImage } from "../data/images"
---

<section
  id="the-river"
  class="relative bg-background py-section"
  aria-labelledby="river-heading"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-landing px-container-x sm:px-8 xl:px-14">
    <!-- Editorial phrase -->
    <p
      class="reveal mb-6 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted"
    >
      The Danube
    </p>

    <h2
      id="river-heading"
      class="reveal max-w-heading font-display text-headline-1 font-bold leading-[1.05] text-foreground"
    >
      The River Between Us
    </h2>

    <p
      class="reveal mt-6 max-w-copy text-base leading-relaxed text-muted sm:text-lg"
    >
      The Danube does not divide Budapest. It tells its story. For centuries,
      the river has been the axis around which two cities breathe — Buda on the
      western hills, Pest on the eastern plains — joined not by geography but by
      the bridges, the light, and the memories that travel between them.
    </p>

    <!-- Danube aerial photo — full width -->
    <figure class="reveal mt-16 sm:mt-20">
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-sm">
        <img
          src={`${danubeImage.src}&w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80`}
          srcset={`${danubeImage.src}&w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 800w, ${danubeImage.src}&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 1200w, ${danubeImage.src}&w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 1600w`}
          sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 90vw, 1200px"
          alt={danubeImage.alt}
          title={`Photo by ${danubeImage.author} on Unsplash`}
          width={danubeImage.width}
          height={danubeImage.height}
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          class="photo-tone w-full object-cover"
        />
      </div>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted">
        Photo by <a
          href={danubeImage.authorUrl}
          class="underline hover:text-foreground"
          rel="noopener">{danubeImage.author}</a
        >
        on <a
          href={danubeImage.unsplashUrl}
          class="underline hover:text-foreground"
          rel="noopener">Unsplash</a
        >
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <!-- Three narrative beats: Buda / Danube / Pest -->
    <div class="mt-20 grid gap-16 sm:mt-28 lg:grid-cols-3 lg:gap-12">
      <!-- Buda -->
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted/60">01</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-headline-3 font-bold text-foreground">
          Buda
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The western bank rises in wooded hills crowned by the Castle District.
          Cobblestone streets lead past Matthias Church, through the turrets of
          Fisherman's Bastion, to viewpoints that hold the entire city in one
          gaze. Buda is memory, stone, and silence.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- The Danube -->
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted/60">02</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-headline-3 font-bold text-foreground">
          The Danube
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Europe's second longest river flows through Budapest for 28
          kilometers, carrying boats, reflections, and seven centuries of
          history beneath its bridges. At sunset the water turns from steel to
          gold, and the city on either side seems to breathe with the same tide.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Pest -->
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted/60">03</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-headline-3 font-bold text-foreground">
          Pest
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The eastern bank spreads outward in grand avenues, Beaux-Arts
          apartment buildings, and the unmistakable silhouette of Parliament.
          Pest is motion, commerce, and conversation — the cafes, the markets,
          the theaters, the life that a city generates when it looks forward.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Buda Castle photo — asymmetric composition -->
    <div class="reveal mt-20 grid gap-8 sm:mt-28 lg:grid-cols-5 lg:gap-12">
      <figure class="lg:col-span-3">
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-sm">
          <img
            src={`${budaCastleImage.src}&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80`}
            srcset={`${budaCastleImage.src}&w=600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 600w, ${budaCastleImage.src}&w=900&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 900w, ${budaCastleImage.src}&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 1200w`}
            sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 90vw, 720px"
            alt={budaCastleImage.alt}
            title={`Photo by ${budaCastleImage.author} on Unsplash`}
            width={budaCastleImage.width}
            height={budaCastleImage.height}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            class="photo-tone aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted">
          Photo by <a
            href={budaCastleImage.authorUrl}
            class="underline hover:text-foreground"
            rel="noopener">{budaCastleImage.author}</a
          >
          on <a
            href={budaCastleImage.unsplashUrl}
            class="underline hover:text-foreground"
            rel="noopener">Unsplash</a
          >
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="flex flex-col justify-center lg:col-span-2">
        <blockquote
          class="font-display text-headline-3 font-bold italic leading-snug text-foreground"
        >
          "Two shores. One soul."
        </blockquote>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The Castle District has watched over the Danube since the 13th
          century. Rebuilt after every war, it remains the hill where Budapest
          remembers what it has been — and what it intends to become.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
